			(at 810.26 53.34 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes)))
		(property "Note" "EN = DRV_EN, EN* = GND. DRV_EN is tied to +3V3 through the fitted link R_DRVEN_ON, so the drivers are always on. Move the link to R_DRVEN_PRSNT to gate them on the far end being present and powered instead, which saves about 60 mA with no cable - but only if your cable actually wires the sidebands, because the no-sideband cable variant exists and would leave the link dead."
			(at 810.26 53.34 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes)))
		(property "Description" "Quad LVDS driver, 400 Mbps, SOIC-16. THE FORWARD GROUP: 153.6 MHz forward clock plus ADC data lanes 0, 1 and 2 at 307.2 Mbit/s each. Three lanes DDR at 153.6 MHz is 921.6 Mbit/s, the complete raw 12-bit 76.8 MSPS stream. All four channels used, none spare"
			(at 810.26 53.34 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes)))
