			(at 914.4 53.34 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes)))
		(property "Note" "EN = DRV_EN, EN* = GND. DRV_EN is tied to +3V3 through the fitted link R_DRVEN_ON, so the drivers are always on. Move the link to R_DRVEN_PRSNT to gate them on the far end being present and powered instead, which saves about 60 mA with no cable - but only if your cable actually wires the sidebands, because the no-sideband cable variant exists and would leave the link dead."
			(at 914.4 53.34 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes)))
		(property "Description" "Quad LVDS driver, 400 Mbps, SOIC-16. Channel 1 is the DUPLICATE forward clock, fed from the same translated net as the primary: the forward clock is the single point of failure for the whole receive path, the far end has spare pins and trains whichever lane works, and this costs one trace. Channels 2 and 3 are the auxiliary transmit pair, channel 4 is a spare brought out to test pads"
			(at 914.4 53.34 0)
			(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes)))
